    "https://www.presby.edu/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/employment/assistant-professor-of-chemistry/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry | Presbyterian College Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\r\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Assistant Professor of Assistant Professor of Chemistry Assistant Professor of Chemistry About PC Offices & Services Human Resources Employment Assistant Professor of Chemistry Assistant Professor of Chemistry Position Description The Presbyterian College Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor level starting August 2027. This position is fully on-site with in-person lecture and laboratory instruction. Teaching expectations include Organic Chemistry with a combination of General Chemistry, and/or upper-level elective courses in the field of the candidate’s expertise. The successful candidates will also be expected to contribute to the undergraduate research program. The candidate will have the opportunity to be supported by the College’s NIH-funded South Carolina-INBRE research program, as an advisor in our PC Summer Fellows research program, and pursue other external funding. Minimum Requirements At a minimum, candidates should have a Ph.D. in Organic, Bioorganic, Medicinal, or related areas of chemistry. (ABD considered). To Apply Interested individuals should electronically send a single PDF containing a cover letter that describes your motivation for applying for this position; curriculum vitae ; statement of teaching philosophy; three letters of recommendation; and (official or unofficial) college and graduate transcripts to Provost Dr. Erin McAdams at [email protected] . For specific questions regarding the position, please contact Dr. A. Craig Powell, chair of the Chemistry Department, at [email protected] . Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. About Presbyterian College Presbyterian College (PC) is a liberal arts college affiliated with the Presbyterian Church USA. The college is committed to an equitable and inclusive learning environment for all students, supports academic freedom, and encourages community involvement. Located in Clinton, South Carolina, PC is approximately 40 minutes from Greenville and Spartanburg, and about one hour from Columbia. The region offers abundant opportunities for social and recreational activities, with easy access to Asheville and Charlotte, North Carolina, and Atlanta, Georgia. Presbyterian College is an EEO employer and does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status, or genetic information. PC is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from minorities and women. Learn More About PC About PC History, Mission, & Plan Benefits & Resources Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Information Campus Police Presbyterian College is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive online experience. If you are unable to access any part of this website due to a disability, please contact Accessible Education at [email protected] for assistance. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATORY POLICY AS TO STUDENTS: Presbyterian College is an equal educational opportunity institution. The College’s admission standards and practices are free from discrimination on the basis of age, sex, race, creed, color, disability, ethnicity or national origin. Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community"
